---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Corrections"
  description="How to report incorrect wording, browser data links, feature definitions, or calculations."
>
  <header class="shell page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">Corrections</span>
    <h1>Report a correction.</h1>
    <p>
      Include the security feature, browser and version, current result, expected result, and a
      reliable source that supports the correction. Technical reports can also include the MDN data
      path and package version.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="shell reading-layout">
    <nav class="page-contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <span class="eyebrow">In this section</span>
      <a href="#section-1">Report a problem with ControlCurrent</a>
      <a href="#section-2">Report a problem with the source data</a>
    </nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2 id="section-1">Report a problem with ControlCurrent</h2>
      <p>
        Use the repository issue tracker for catalogue mappings, calculations, wording,
        accessibility, or reproducibility. Do not include private application details or security
        vulnerabilities in a public issue.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/slicedearth/controlcurrent/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Open the ControlCurrent issue tracker
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="section-2">Report a problem with the source data</h2>
      <p>
        A BCD support-data problem should also be reported through the MDN Browser Compatibility
        Data contribution process. ControlCurrent will not silently override source evidence with an
        undocumented local claim.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Open the MDN BCD issue tracker
        </a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
